# Reference papers

Before proposing or re-deriving a geometry / simulation method, skim
[`reference/MANIFEST.md`](reference/MANIFEST.md) by **tags** and keywords.

## Workflow

1. Match the topic to manifest tags (e.g. `hepworth`, `ARAP`, `winding`, `TP`, `fluids`).
2. Read the entry **summary** and **maps_to** first.
3. Open the local PDF under [`reference/`](reference/) only when implementing details
   (energies, local/global steps, discretizations).
4. Cite the paper by title + local filename when discussing design choices.

## Adding papers

1. Place PDF in `reference/` (prefer `authorYEAR-short-slug.pdf`).
2. Append a MANIFEST entry: title, file, url, tags, summary, maps_to.
3. Record URL/DOI in `reference/SOURCES.txt`.
4. Optional: add a fetch line to `scripts/fetch_reference_papers.sh`.

PDFs may later move to external storage; keep **MANIFEST.md** (and SOURCES) in-repo
as the searchable index.
